=== demo

  MethodCache, a guided tour
  Add caching to any .NET method with one attribute. Every number below is measured live.

  1. One attribute
  ────────────────
  Put [Cache] on an interface method and call AddMethodCache(). The source generator writes the decorator.

    public interface IWeatherService
    {
        [Cache(Duration = "00:05:00", Tags = ["weather"])]
        Task<Forecast> GetForecastAsync(string city);
    }

    services.AddSingleton<IWeatherService, WeatherService>();
    services.AddMethodCache();

    First call (runs the method)        420.4 ms
    Second call (from the cache)          0.5 ms
    Average of 1,000,000 cached calls     448 ns
    Resolved type                     IWeatherServiceDecorator
    ✓ The second call returned the same result without running the method
    ✓ WeatherService ran once for 1,100,002 calls

  2. Stampede protection
  ──────────────────────
  100 requests ask for the same uncached value at the same moment. Only one of them runs the method.

    100 concurrent calls finished in    404.7 ms
    ✓ WeatherService ran once
    ✓ All 100 callers got the same result

  3. Tags that understand your arguments
  ──────────────────────────────────────
  "user:{userId}" becomes user:1, user:2 ... Renaming user 1 invalidates user 1 and nothing else.

    [Cache(Duration = "00:10:00", Tags = ["users", "user:{userId}"])]
    Task<UserProfile> GetProfileAsync(int userId);

    [CacheInvalidate(Tags = ["user:{userId}"])]
    Task RenameAsync(int userId, string newName);

    Load users 1 and 2, twice each    2 database queries
    Rename user 1, load both again    1 new database query
    ✓ User 1 is fresh: Ada King
    ✓ User 2 still came from the cache: Alan Turing

  4. Change policies without touching code
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Durations can come from the attribute, a global default, appsettings.json (reloaded live) or a runtime override.

    services.AddMethodCache(config => config.Defaults(o => o.WithDuration(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10))));
    services.AddMethodCacheFromConfiguration(configuration);   // the "MethodCache" section

    At startup:
    Method                            Duration  Comes from
    IProductCatalog.GetPriceAsync     30 s      startup-fluent, attributes
    IProductCatalog.GetProductAsync   15 min    startup-fluent, attributes, configuration-files
    IWeatherService.GetForecastAsync  5 min     startup-fluent, attributes

    After editing appsettings.json (15 → 20 min):
    Method                            Duration  Comes from
    IProductCatalog.GetPriceAsync     30 s      startup-fluent, attributes
    IProductCatalog.GetProductAsync   20 min    startup-fluent, attributes, configuration-files
    IWeatherService.GetForecastAsync  5 min     startup-fluent, attributes

    ✓ appsettings.json was reloaded while the app was running
    Runtime override, then a call     entry MethodCache.Demo.IProductCatalog.GetProductAsync:KB-1 lives 1 min
    ✓ The runtime override applied to new entries at once
    ✓ Clearing the override restored the appsettings.json value

  5. Cache code you don't own
  ───────────────────────────
  IFxRatesClient comes from a vendor's package. One line caches its rate lookups; orders still reach the API.

    [assembly: CacheInterface(typeof(IFxRatesClient), nameof(IFxRatesClient.GetRateAsync),
        Duration = "00:01:00", Tags = ["fx", "fx:{from}"])]

    services.AddSingleton<IFxRatesClient, FxRatesClient>();   // the vendor's client, as usual

    Three lookups of EUR → SEK          255.5 ms
    ✓ The exchange-rate API was called once
    ✓ PlaceOrderAsync isn't listed, so both orders reached the API

  6. See what is cached
  ─────────────────────
  ICacheAdministrator (and the MethodCache.AspNetCore endpoints) show stats and live entries, and can invalidate them.

    Hits / misses                     1,100,105 / 7  (hit ratio 100.0 %)
    Entries                           5
    Key                                                          Expires in  Tags
    FxVendor.IFxRatesClient.GetRateAsync:EUR:SEK                 60 s        fx, fx:EUR
    MethodCache.Demo.IUserProfiles.GetProfileAsync:1             9.9 min     users, user:1
    MethodCache.Demo.IUserProfiles.GetProfileAsync:2             9.9 min     users, user:2
    MethodCache.Demo.IWeatherService.GetForecastAsync:Malmö      4.9 min     weather
    MethodCache.Demo.IWeatherService.GetForecastAsync:Stockholm  4.9 min     weather

    Invalidate tag "weather"          2 → 0 entries
    ✓ Every hit and miss is counted, including the million in chapter 1
    ✓ Tag invalidation removed every weather entry

  All 6 chapters behaved as described.

  Next: the README has the full feature list, and samples/MethodCache.WebDemo shows the same
